This Python script creates a `BluetoothConnection` class to handle the connection and communication with the Bluetooth device. It uses the `serial` library to establish a connection and send commands. The script sets up a signal handler for `SIGINT` (which is triggered by pressing Ctrl+C) to ensure graceful termination and proper cleanup.

